# A Case's "To solve" is an intervening-if trigger (CR 603.4, 719.3a): "if this Case is not solved" is asked again as it
# resolves. Bot1 gains 5 life from five Ornithopters entering under Case of the Uneaten Feast, and at its end step copies the
# "To solve" trigger with Return the Favor. The copy resolves first and solves the Case; the trigger itself then finds the
# Case solved and does nothing. The Case is solved, once.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Case of the Uneaten Feast
Black Lotus
Return the Favor
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Plains x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Case of the Uneaten Feast.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T5 Bot1.End]
? Bot1.Life = 25
? Stack = Case of the Uneaten Feast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Return the Favor.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Copy target)
Bot1.Target(Stack.Case of the Uneaten Feast)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Case of the Uneaten Feast.Solved = true
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
[T6 Bot2.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Case of the Uneaten Feast.Solved = true
Bot1.Graveyard = Return the Favor; Black Lotus
